abstract: >-
  NOETHER is a two-layer framework for metamorphic relation (MR) identification.
  The upstream layer is an eight-block decomposition over recurrent mathematical
  structures (symmetry, order, self-adjoint, time-reversal, limit,
  qualitative-dynamics, method-comparison, relational equivalence), stated as
  an empirical hypothesis. The downstream layer is the CONSTRUCT-MP algorithm
  with two formal guarantees: algebraic closure under the Translate operator
  (Theorem 1) and polynomial-time decidability under a finite generating set
  (Theorem 2). The framework is instantiated on three structurally distinct
  operator algebras (Boltzmann reactor physics, equivariant machine learning,
  relational query optimisers) and the absolute-completeness conjecture
  (Theorem 1') is falsified on a fourth program family (PWR core diffusion)
  via two pairwise-independent counterexamples.
keywords:
  - metamorphic testing
  - operator algebras
  - metamorphic relation identification
  - scientific computing
  - equivariant machine learning
  - Boltzmann transport
  - PWR core diffusion
